ns on every suite. I weakened production `SyncFrom` five ways, and the four the brief named each fail that test when run alone:\n- audit only when the peer and local sets are the same size;\n- audit only when the peer holds nothing the local lacks;\n- audit only the first namespace;\n- audit only the first sync round.\n\nA harmless control change survived, which proves the check can report a survivor.\n\n**One blocking finding, the same class as rev3 at an adjacent site:**\n- **What survives:** changing `SyncFrom` to byte-check only the first shared object in each namespace (`common = common[:1]`). The full `go test ./internal/merkleinventory` still passes.\n- **Why:** the generated product test skips itself unless you run it with a subtest selector, and the always-run test never puts two shared objects in one namespace.\n- **Proof the property exists:** the product shard `N3` does catch this change (32 failures), but nothing in the configured suite runs it.\n- **Asked of the producer:** make the configured suite measure this, with either an always-on small shard of the generated conflict cases or a named test where the conflicting object is not the first shared one. They must also ship this change and a \"last object only\" variant as harness rows, and remove a Python build artifact that was left in the candidate.\n\n**Required reruns:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Registry digest | Matches the pinned value; editing the registry makes tracecheck fail |\n| Full `go test ./...` on the exact tree | 45 of 46 packages ok on the archive copy; the one failure, `specpin`, needs the board directory, and it passes in the live worktree |\n| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` | Clean; gofmt clean |\n| README coverage | A wrong figure makes the README coverage test fail |\n| Importer comparison (28 packages, base vs candidate) | No failures in the candidate. Some tombstone tests were removed because tombstones went from unsupported to supported, as reviewed in the earlier Story leaf. Two tmuxserver test names changed; they encode scratch-path length, so no behaviour moved. |\n| Determinism (`-count=3`) | Passes on the new tests and on product shard `N2` |\n| Registry decoded | All three Story cases are in their clause lists; no trunk case or row was lost |\n| `task-board.config.json` | Byte-identical to base |\n\n**Non-blocking notes:**\n- The syntax-tree check for \"audit is unconditional\" missed all four of my changes that weakened how the shared-object list is built. Only the behaviour test caught them.\n- I did not rerun the shipped mutation harness; my own plants replaced it for this round.\n\nI deleted the scratch directory and added this round's lesson to the existing memory note on conflict-case coverage.","ttft_ms":2185,"type":"result","duration_ms":1155866,"uuid":"1103e872-e1b0-4939-95e4-fd585486829d","ttft_stream_ms":1680,"time_to_request_ms":46,"first_content_frame_ms":1680,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
